## 2. Primary Relationships

```text
Universities (1)   ──► Departments (Many)
Universities (1)   ──► Users (Many)
Users (Many)       ◄─► Roles (Many)           -- via user_roles_join
Hackathons (1)     ──► Teams (Many)
Teams (Many)       ◄─► Users (Many)           -- via team_members (Roster)
Teams (1)          ──► Problem Statement (1)  -- Strict One-to-One
Problem Spec (1)   ──► Pain Points (Many)
Teams (1)          ──► Solution Concepts (Many)
Solutions (1)      ──► Idea Votes (Many)      -- Cast by team members
Teams (1)          ──► Tasks (Many)
Tasks (1)          ──► Comments (Many)
Teams (1)          ──► Documents (Many)
Documents (1)      ──► Doc Versions (Many)
Teams (1)          ──► Presentation (1)       -- Strict One-to-One
```

---

## 3. Core Application Data Flow

### A. User Registration Flow
```text
Validate University Domain (universities)
  └─► Insert new user credentials (users)
       └─► Assign 'Student' role (user_roles_join)
            └─► Initialize settings (settings)
```

### B. Create Team Flow
```text
Insert team metadata (teams)
  └─► Add leader to roster (team_members)
       └─► Log action event (activity_logs)
```

### C. Task Progress Flow
```text
Update task status to 'completed' (tasks)
  └─► Recalculate team progress (PL/pgSQL trigger)
       └─► Update progress percentage (teams)
            └─► Log task update (activity_logs)
```

### D. Submission & Review Flow
```text
Upload PRESENTATIONS (write path to version table)
  └─► Faculty inserts grades in JUDGE_REVIEWS
```
